     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5 to 10 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock, and an overdose of this size can be life-threatening. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from a licensed clinician who can check the dose against the patient's chart.\n\nPlease ask the treating clinician to confirm the intended dose. If they want 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it once they confirm. If they really do intend 50 mg, they should enter it themselves and document the rationale, and pharmacy should verify it."
      }
